? entitled(Bela, event { believe() }).
# => TRUE

# And conviction no longer confers personhood. Note Article 1 has a second route
# since release landed — `free -> person` — but that one needs somebody to write
# a fact, so conviction remains the only route into rights-bearing status that
# needs nobody's permission, and this fixture removes it. Zed's conviction and
# T3 custody evidence are written HERE (this file used to query him bare, which
# was the weak kind of FALSE the taxonomy warns about): convicted under an
# active, case-bound, independently observed lease, and no longer a person.
injure(Zed, Ivo).
judge(Court, Zed).
cite(Court, Case_Zed, Zed).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Zed, CaseScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Zed, CaseScope).
observe(Chronicle, Case_Zed, Court, HolderScope).
observe(TemporalReview, Case_Zed, Court, HolderScope).
